 "findings": [
  {
   "evidence": "grep for `\u21d1(unitSphereRiemannianIsometry` / `coe_unitSphereRiemannianIsometry` in TauCeti returns only the inline `have hcoe` at Isometry/Sphere.lean:86 and the pointwise `coe_unitSphereRiemannianIsometry_apply` at :101; the analogous function-level lemma exists in the Euclidean file (`coe_toRiemannianIsometry`, Isometry/Euclidean.lean:88-89) and `Diffeomorph.coe_toEquiv` is @[simp] in the opposite direction.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Geometry/Manifold/Riemannian/Isometry/Sphere.lean",
   "fix": "Add `@[simp] theorem coe_unitSphereRiemannianIsometry (e : E \u2243\u2097\u1d62[\u211d] F) : \u21d1(unitSphereRiemannianIsometry (n := n) (k := k) e) = unitSphereEquiv e := (rfl)` and use it in place of the inline `hcoe`, mirroring `AffineIsometryEquiv.coe_toRiemannianIsometry` in Isometry/Euclidean.lean:89. Alternatively (or additionally) restate the key identity directly for the isometry, with `mfderiv (\ud835\udce1 n) (\ud835\udce1 k) (unitSphereRiemannianIsometry e) x v` on the left, so the ambient differential of the exported object is reachable without unfolding.",
   "issue": "`mvfderiv_coe_sphere_unitSphereEquiv` (@[simp]) is keyed on `unitSphereEquiv e`, but the object the file exports is `unitSphereRiemannianIsometry e` / `unitSphereIsomHom e`, and no lemma relates their coercions: the only coe lemmas are the pointwise `coe_unitSphereRiemannianIsometry_apply` (line 101) and `unitSphereRiemannianIsometry_apply` (line 107). The author needed exactly the missing fact and inlined it as `have hcoe : \u21d1(unitSphereDiffeomorph e \u221e) = unitSphereEquiv e` (lines 86-87), proved by `rw [\u2190 Diffeomorph.coe_toEquiv, unitSphereDiffeomorph_toEquiv]` \u2014 i.e. against the simp direction of `Diffeomorph.coe_toEquiv` (Mathlib/Geometry/Manifold/Diffeomorph.lean:145-146), so simp cannot reconstruct it. Consequence: with `TauCeti.norm_tangentSpace_sphere` and `inner_tangentSpace_sphere` marked @[simp] (Sphere.lean:93,102), simp unfolds any sphere-tangent `\u2016v\u2016`/`inner \u211d v w` into `mvfderiv` form, the key identity then fails to match, and goals such as `\u2016mfderiv (\ud835\udce1 n) (\ud835\udce1 n) (unitSphereIsomHom e) x v\u2016 = \u2016v\u2016` \u2014 closed by the generic `RiemannianIsometry.norm_mfderiv`/`inner_mfderiv` (Isometry/Basic.lean:76,83, both @[simp]) \u2014 are left in an unprovable `mvfderiv` form depending on which of the two colliding simp lemmas wins the tie-break.",
   "line": "66"
  }
 ],
